Diagnostics: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines runtime diagnostics policy — how AI analyzes runtime
  problems, correlates signals, and identifies root causes.

DiagnosticFlow:
  Alert/Incident
    ↓
  CollectSignals:
    - Metrics (RED/USE/business)
    - Logs (structured, time-range)
    - Traces (request path)
    - Deploy history
    - Code changes
    - Dependency status
    ↓
  CorrelateSignals:
    - Time correlation
    - Service dependency correlation
    - Deploy correlation
    ↓
  IdentifyPattern:
    - Known pattern match
    - Anomaly detection
    - Regression detection
    ↓
  RootCause:
    - Confirmed root cause
    - Confidence level
    - Evidence chain

ConfidenceLevels:
  CONFIRMED:
    - Multiple evidence sources agree
    - Reproducible
    - Action clear
  HIGH_CONFIDENCE:
    - Strong evidence
    - Likely correct
    - Action clear
  LIKELY:
    - Good evidence
    - Probable cause
    - Action proposed
  POSSIBLE:
    - Weak evidence
    - Multiple candidates
    - Further investigation needed
  UNKNOWN:
    - Insufficient data
    - Escalate to human

DiagnosticTools:
  - Metric analysis (trends, anomalies)
  - Log analysis (error patterns, correlation)
  - Trace analysis (bottleneck identification)
  - Deploy diff (code change impact)
  - Dependency graph (cascade analysis)

CrossLayer:
  Incident: Diagnostic output feeds incident record
  Task: Root cause creates task for fix
  Architecture: Recurring patterns trigger architecture review
  Security: Security events feed security incident process

